      <title>Suit alleges Louisiana land deal between SpaceX and ExxonMobil violates open meetings law</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/26/louisiana-spacex-exxonmobil-land-deal-lawsuit</link>
      <description>Suit says parish board was manipulated to allow deal to go through and settlement agreement hidden from public After ending a lawsuit over ExxonMobil ’s damage to wetlands, Louisiana officials moved quickly to approve a deal giving SpaceX access to 125,000 acres (50,600 hectares) of marsh formerly owned by the oil company. A new lawsuit now alleges they did so in violation of the state’s open meetings law. The lawsuit, filed by three south-central Louisiana residents, follows state and…</description>
