      <title>Britain’s sex slump, nuclear weapons in space, key suspect in bowel cancer rise – podcast</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/science/audio/2026/nov/26/britains-sex-slump-nuclear-weapons-in-space-key-suspect-in-bowel-cancer-rise-podcast</link>
      <description>Madeleine Finlay and co-host Ian Sample discuss the three science stories you need to know about this week, including a breakdown of what the average Briton is – or isn’t – up to in the bedroom. They also discuss what detonating a nuclear weapon in space could mean for everyone on Earth and how a bacterial toxin might be contributing to a rise in cases of some early-onset bowel cancers. ‘Not about notches on bedpost’: people in Great Britain having less sex – especially young adults Germany…</description>
