      <title>Nasa knocked an asteroid off course. New closeup photos shed light on aftermath</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/25/dimorphos-asteroid-spacecraft-crash-closeup-images</link>
      <description>Images of Dimorphos four years on from crash could help scientists design potential planetary defence system Humanity may not yet have a means of fending off a Vogon constructor fleet – the destroyers of Earth in The Hitchhiker’s Guide to the Galaxy – but its prospects of surviving an encounter with a rogue asteroid are looking considerably brighter. Four years after Nasa deliberately slammed a spacecraft into a roughly 160-metre-wide asteroid called Dimorphos to knock it off course…</description>
