      <title>Trump administration approves Elon Musk’s plan for datacenters in space</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/25/spacex-datacenter-satellites-approval</link>
      <description>The FCC approved 1m Starmind satellites, with the deployment of 100,000 no later than November 2035 US federal regulators approved a constellation of datacenters to process data in space on Wednesday, saying that they would “support America’s booming super intelligence economy”. The Federal Communications Commission (FCC) said in a statement that regulators had approved 1m Starmind orbital satellites, or compute modules, built by Elon Musk’s SpaceX. It is the first such authorization in US…</description>
